change-remote
  short: Changes the remote address used in the tunnel for the provided vpn addr
  help: 
  flags:
  -address string
    	The new remote address, ip:port
close-tunnel
  short: Closes a tunnel for the provided vpn addr
  help: 
  flags:
  -local-only
    	Disables notifying the remote that the tunnel is shutting down
create-tunnel
  short: Creates a tunnel for the provided vpn address
  help: The lighthouses will be queried for real addresses but you can provide one as well.
  flags:
  -address string
    	Optionally provide a real remote address, ip:port 
device-info
  short: Prints information about the network device.
  help: 
  flags:
  -json
    	outputs as json with more information
  -pretty
    	pretty prints json, assumes -json
help
  short: prints available commands or help <command> for specific usage info
  help: 
list-hostmap
  short: List all known previously connected hosts
  help: 
  flags:
  -by-index
    	gets all hosts in the hostmap from the index table
  -json
    	outputs as json with more information
  -pretty
    	pretty prints json, assumes -json
list-lighthouse-addrmap
  short: List all lighthouse map entries
  help: 
  flags:
  -json
    	outputs as json with more information
  -pretty
    	pretty prints json, assumes -json
list-pending-hostmap
  short: List all handshaking hosts
  help: 
  flags:
  -by-index
    	gets all hosts in the hostmap from the index table
  -json
    	outputs as json with more information
  -pretty
    	pretty prints json, assumes -json
log-format
  short: Gets or sets the current log format
  help: 
log-level
  short: Gets or sets the current log level
  help: 
print-cert
  short: Prints the current certificate being used or the certificate for the provided vpn addr
  help: 
  flags:
  -json
    	outputs as json
  -pretty
    	pretty prints json, assumes -json
  -raw
    	raw prints the PEM encoded certificate, not compatible with -json or -pretty
print-relays
  short: Prints json details about all relay info
  help: 
  flags:
  -pretty
    	pretty prints json
print-tunnel
  short: Prints json details about a tunnel for the provided vpn addr
  help: 
  flags:
  -pretty
    	pretty prints json
query-lighthouse
  short: Query the lighthouses for the provided vpn address
  help: This command is asynchronous. Only currently known udp addresses will be printed.
reload
  short: Reloads configuration from disk, same as sending HUP to the process
  help: 
version
  short: Prints the currently running version of nebula
  help: 
